course: dictionary
lesson: 10626
title: Unfold: opening out and events
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unfold is a verb. Its opposite is fold. When you fold something, you bend it over itself. When you unfold it, you open it out so it lies flat or spreads out again. «Unfold a map» means open the map so you can see all of it.
explain: The word also works for stories and news. «Watch events unfold» means watch things happen, one after another, and learn about them little by little. To tell which meaning is meant, read the words around it: a map is paper you open, but events are things that happen.
explain: Nature uses the same idea. In the text about the ladybird, «thin wings unfold from underneath» the hard red shell, so the wings open out from where they were folded up. Scientists also use the word for tiny changes, like «Heat unfolds the long protein molecules in egg white».
fact: Unfold means to open something that was folded, so it lies flat or spreads out.
fact: «Unfold a map» and «unfold a towel» both mean open out.
fact: «As the story unfolds» means the story is revealed bit by bit.
fact: «Watch events unfold» means watch things happen and become known little by little.
fact: Some folded things can be unfolded and are still the same material: «fold a paper aeroplane and unfold it, and it is still paper».
exercise: «Unfold a map» means what? | Tear it into pieces | Draw a new map | *Open a folded map so it lies flat | Fold it up small
exercise: «Watch events unfold.» In this phrase, what does unfold mean? | Fold up neatly | Break into pieces | *Happen and become known little by little | Stay still and quiet
exercise: The ladybird's «thin wings unfold from underneath» its shell. What is happening to the wings? | *They open out from where they were folded up | They fall off | They turn red | They get wet
test: «As the story unfolds, the children learn the truth.» What does as the story unfolds suggest? | The story is finished and thrown away | *The story is revealed bit by bit | The story is printed in red | The story is read only once
test: Which example in the text shows a change that can be undone? | Lime juice turning fish white | A ladybird's shell splitting down the middle | *Folding a paper aeroplane and unfolding it, and it is still paper | Heat unfolding egg white proteins for good
exam: In «Heat unfolds the long protein molecules in egg white so they tangle together for good», what does for good suggest? | The molecules are folded up again later | *The change is permanent and cannot be easily undone | The egg white will change back easily | The egg white is only warmed for a short time
